    <article class="container">
        <h1>Pilates Sculpt in Lagos</h1>
        <p style="color:#aaa; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:40px;">High-intensity mat Pilates meets resistance training. Where Pilates meets power.</p>
        
        <h2>What Is Pilates Sculpt?</h2>
        <p>Pilates Sculpt is where classical mat Pilates meets high-intensity resistance training. We take the core principles of Pilates — control, precision, breath — and add light resistance, higher repetitions, and faster transitions to create a class that builds strength, burns calories, and transforms your body.</p>
        
        <p>Think of it as Pilates with an edge. The movements are still controlled and intentional, but the pace is quicker, the burn is deeper, and the results are faster.</p>
        
        <div class="highlight-box">
            <h3>The Sculpt Difference</h3>
            <p>Traditional mat Pilates builds strength through bodyweight resistance and slow, controlled movements. Pilates Sculpt adds:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Light resistance:</strong> Small weights, resistance bands, and gliders</li>
                <li><strong>Higher reps:</strong> 12-20 repetitions per exercise instead of 5-8</li>
                <li><strong>Faster transitions:</strong> Less rest, more work, higher heart rate</li>
                <li><strong>Cardio integration:</strong> Bursts of movement that elevate your heart rate</li>
                <li><strong>Muscle fatigue:</strong> The burn that creates real change</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The result? A class that feels like Pilates but works like strength training.</p>
        </div>
        
        <h2>The Class Experience</h2>
        <p>Our Pilates Sculpt classes follow a structured format that maximizes results:</p>
        
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Dynamic warm-up:</strong> Movement prep that activates your core and raises your body temperature</li>
            <li><strong>Arm series:</strong> Light weights target shoulders, biceps, triceps, and upper back</li>
            <li><strong>Core series:</strong> Classical Pilates with added resistance — the hundred, roll-ups, leg lowers, teasers</li>
            <li><strong>Glute series:</strong> Side-lying and prone work that lifts and shapes your backside</li>
            <li><strong>Thigh series:</strong> Standing and floor work that targets quads, hamstrings, and inner/outer thighs</li>
            <li><strong>Cardio bursts:</strong> Short intervals of high-intensity movement to spike your heart rate</li>
            <li><strong>Final stretch:</strong> Deep release and integration</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>Classes are 50-60 minutes and suitable for intermediate to advanced practitioners. Beginners are welcome but should expect a challenge.</p>
        
        <h2>The Heat Advantage</h2>
        <p>Our 30-32°C infrared heat makes Pilates Sculpt even more effective:</p>
        
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Increased flexibility:</strong> Warm muscles allow deeper range of motion</li>
            <li><strong>Enhanced circulation:</strong> Blood flow delivers more oxygen to working muscles</li>
            <li><strong>Greater calorie burn:</strong> Your body works harder to cool itself</li>
            <li><strong>Detoxification:</strong> Deep sweating releases toxins and reduces bloating</li>
            <li><strong>Reduced injury risk:</strong> Warm tissues are less prone to strain</li>
            <li><strong>Enhanced recovery:</strong> The heat soothes muscles as you work them</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Who Is This For?</h2>
        <p>Pilates Sculpt is for people who want results:</p>
        
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Strength seekers:</strong> Build lean muscle without bulk</li>
            <li><strong>Weight loss:</strong> High-intensity format burns calories during and after class</li>
            <li><strong>Athletes:</strong> Cross-training that builds core stability and prevents injury</li>
            <li><strong>Pilates graduates:</strong> Take your mat practice to the next level</li>
            <li><strong>Busy people:</strong> Maximum results in minimum time</li>
            <li><strong>Tourists:</strong> Sweat out the travel, tighten up for the beach</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2>Pricing</h2>
        <p><strong>Drop-In:</strong> €22 (buy 1, get 1 free for first-timers)<br>
        <strong>Vacation Week:</strong> €59 unlimited<br>
        <strong>Intro Offer:</strong> €79 for 14 days unlimited</p>
        
        <a href="mailto:hello@heatlagos.com?subject=Pilates Sculpt Class Booking" class="btn">Book Your First Class</a>
        
